Old Marrow squats on a stone that is probably a stone, watching you with one good eye and one that has opinions.
"New blood. The marsh told me. The marsh tells me everything — mostly complaints, mostly about me."
"Everything down here is somebody's leftover god, child. Catch the small ones first."
"The big ones? The big ones catch you. Gentle hands — the gods had those once. Look how that ended for them."
[You feel marked. Not cursed, exactly. Filed.]
"Go on, then. The Rust Marsh keeps a ledger, and your page is looking thin."
